      <div class="article__main">
        <div class="article__body prose">
          <blockquote>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Before you play: <strong>212 GB+ free</strong>, pre-load done, controller charged. In game: expect <strong>30 FPS</strong>, <strong>heavy Vice City traffic</strong> and <strong>six-star wanted levels</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Confirmed vs old habits:</strong> tips marked <em>Confirmed</em> come from official sources or previews. Tips marked <em>Based on previous GTA games</em> may change in GTA 6.</li>
<li><strong>Button names and exact menus are not announced yet.</strong> We will fill them in after launch. We will not guess.</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Words used on this page.</strong> <em>Wanted level</em> is how hard the police chase you. <em>Free roam</em> is playing outside a mission. <em>Series-standard</em> means it was true in earlier GTA games.</p>
<h2 id="before-you-start-confirmed" tabindex="-1">Before you start (Confirmed)</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Free 212 GB+.</strong> PS5: <strong>Settings &gt; Storage</strong>. Xbox: <strong>Xbox button &gt; Profile &amp; system &gt; Settings &gt; System &gt; Storage devices</strong>. See <a href="preload-size.md">pre-load steps</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Finish the pre-load.</strong> PS5: <strong>PS button &gt; Downloads/Uploads</strong>. Xbox: <strong>Xbox button &gt; My games &amp; apps &gt; Queue</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Turn on Rest Mode downloads (PS5).</strong> <strong>Settings &gt; Saved Data and Game/App Settings &gt; Automatic Updates &gt; Auto-Install in Rest Mode</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Share the console?</strong> PS5: <strong>Settings &gt; Users and Accounts &gt; Other &gt; Console Sharing and Offline Play &gt; Enable</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Expect 30 FPS.</strong> No performance mode is announced. See <a href="ps5-settings.md">PS5 settings</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Change the controller buzz if it is too strong.</strong> Rockstar says haptics are adjustable in accessibility settings.</li>
</ol>
<p>![PS5 storage and downloads screens side by side](TODO: image:beginner-tips-step-1 — menu screen, PS5: Settings &gt; Storage and Control Center &gt; Downloads/Uploads)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. The two PS5 screens to check before launch.</em></p>
<h2 id="in-game-what-previews-confirm" tabindex="-1">In game: what previews confirm</h2>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Tip</th>
<th>Why</th>
<th>Source</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Plan escapes in Vice City.</strong> Roads are often busy, and traffic makes it harder to lose the police.</td>
<td>Game Informer preview</td>
<td>Mapheist, citing Game Informer</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Use both leads.</strong> You can switch between Jason and Lucia in free roam and in missions. The button is <strong>not announced</strong>.</td>
<td>Previews</td>
<td>GameSpot, VGC</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Watch your wanted stars.</strong> There are six stars. Crimes show under the stars.</td>
<td>Previews</td>
<td>GameSpot</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Do not wave guns around.</strong> People react and call the police if you carry a gun in public.</td>
<td>Previews</td>
<td>GameSpot</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>New cars may need a “key cloner”.</strong> Older cars may need a slim jim or a smashed window.</td>
<td>Previews</td>
<td>GameSpot, Wikipedia</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Body and looks matter.</strong> Workouts build muscle, food affects weight and bad sleep shows on the face.</td>
<td>Previews</td>
<td>GameSpot, VGC</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Gun limit (reported):</strong> 2 sidearms and 2 long guns. The rest stay in your vehicle.</td>
<td>Previews of the Extended Look. Not yet confirmed in play.</td>
<td>GTA Boom, Hudwire (secondary)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>![diagram of six wanted stars](TODO: image:beginner-tips-step-2 — diagram, our own art: six stars filling from empty to full with the label “wanted level”)
<em>Caption: Diagram. The six-star wanted level.</em></p>
<h2 id="based-on-previous-gta-games-not-confirmed-for-gta-6" tabindex="-1">Based on previous GTA games (not confirmed for GTA 6)</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>To lose the police, break line of sight.</strong> Get out of view, then stay out of view until the stars fade. (Worked in earlier GTA games.)</li>
<li><strong>Keep a fast car close</strong> before you start a risky job. (Earlier GTA games.)</li>
<li><strong>Save before a hard mission</strong> if the game lets you. Earlier GTA games used autosave plus manual saves.</li>
<li><strong>Check the pause menu and map before you spend money.</strong> Earlier games hid shops and settings there.</li>
</ol>
<p>![map pin set with a fast car near a mission marker](TODO: image:beginner-tips-step-3 — map pin, our own art: a mission marker with a car pin beside it)
<em>Caption: Map pin. Park a fast car near the mission marker.</em></p>
<h2 id="not-announced-yet" tabindex="-1">Not announced yet</h2>
<ul>
<li>Money rates, car prices and best early purchases</li>
<li>Difficulty options</li>
<li>Exact button names for switching leads and for each action</li>
</ul>
<p>We will publish money methods, vehicle guides and collectible maps after launch, once players have checked them.</p>
<h2 id="faq" tabindex="-1">FAQ</h2>
<h3 id="is-gta-6-good-for-beginners" tabindex="-1">Is GTA 6 good for beginners?</h3>
<p>Rockstar has not announced difficulty options. We will update this page after launch.</p>
<h3 id="do-i-need-a-subscription-to-play" tabindex="-1">Do I need a subscription to play?</h3>
<p>PlayStation lists GTA VI as single-player with offline play enabled. Subscriptions for online features are not announced.</p>
<h3 id="what-is-the-first-thing-to-do" tabindex="-1">What is the first thing to do?</h3>
<p>Check you have 212 GB+ free and that the pre-load is finished.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-switch-between-jason-and-lucia" tabindex="-1">Can I switch between Jason and Lucia?</h3>
<p>Yes, per previews. The button is not announced.</p>
